WEBVTT

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:13.290
Kylie!

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:15.460
This little guys got a bit of a fever.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.920
Is he one of the kids from your place?

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:17.620
Yeah.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:18.710
What brings you here?

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:20.670
Just a regular checkup.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:23.790
I put mine off for so long 
that the Madame flipped!

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.790
That's cause in our line of work

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.380
we risk running into serious 
accidents if we aren't at our best.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.790
These checkups help keep 
us in peak condition.

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:33.060
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.250
You crash if you get sick?

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.800
Are you gonna die, Reona?

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.830
Miyuri, don't you worry about me.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.380
Soya?

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:42.210
Here!

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:42.960
C'mon, Soya.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.080
I don't wanna get a shot!

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:44.750
Hey!

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:45.920
Miyuri, you wait here.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.170
I'll watch her for you.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.000
Thanks!

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.890
Hey there. I'm Kylie.

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:52.790
I work with Reona.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:56.880
Your job isn't dangerous or anything, is it?

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.080
Well, it's definitely not safe.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.420
Oh, I knew it!

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.790
Why does Reona keep flying 
if she might get hurt?

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:06.670
I think she flies for your sake.

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:07.790
For me?

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:12.000
Everyone's got something they fly to protect.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.170
That's why we don't let 
ourselves get shot down!

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.420
Because we wanna get back 
and see the people we love.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.650
Really...?

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:20.330
Do you have something you fly for, too?

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:21.380
'Course I do!

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:22.330
What is it?

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:23.420
Well, you see!

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:25.210
I...

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:27.290
Huh?

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:47.250
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:51.750
Kumo to kumo amime o nukete

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:55.290
Odoru hane kaze o matou

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:58.750
Me no mae de hoshi ga ochiteiku

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:08.040
Akogareta aoi ao

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:11.080
Nijimu chihyou keriageta

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:16.290
Kikasete yo kimi dake no sora no ne o

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:25.630
Tobidatsu jyuuryoku o mikata ni tsukete

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:32.040
Mou ichido nando demo warai nagara

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:39.080
Bokura wa ushiro o muite tobou to wa shinai

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:44.290
Tsukinai yume asu o otte ikiru

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:47.790
Waita zetsubou ni ai o tozashita

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.080
Yowai boku wa kirai da

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:56.040
Nagareru ima mukau saki wa mirai

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:07.830
So this is a fish?

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.210
I'd never seen one before myself.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:12.460
The Great Airship Robbery

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:11.790
There was nothing like it in See the Sea!

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.040
It was exactly like the 
encyclopedias described.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.170
It's still pretty weird, huh?

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:16.460
Are you feeling constipated?

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:20.130
She's just not too happy 
with today's mission, huh?

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:23.500
You said the pay was incredible, though!

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.250
That's because that fish is worth a fortune.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.570
And because we took a job that should

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:30.730
be handled by multiple teams all on our own.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:33.480
"As the new mayor of Ikesuka, Isao moves to

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:36.820
celebrate the foundation of the 
Brotherhood of Freedom Union.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:40.290
He has purchased a rare fish,
and plans to put it on display for the public."

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:43.820
"He has tasked the Ouni Company's 
KOTOBUKI Corps, heroes of the

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.030
Nanko oil field, with its transportation."

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:47.750
Goodness me...

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:49.460
Did you go take a look at the fish, Johnny?

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:50.080
Nope.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.080
What?! Why? It's really cool, you know!

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.960
It would only bring back memories...

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.170
Of poor Miki...

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:56.630
Here we go again.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:57.250
Who's Miki?

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:02.090
He splurged to get a fish to 
serve at his wedding, see.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:02.710
What?!

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:03.960
So you're married?

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:04.790
You've eaten fish before?!

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:05.670
How was it?!

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:08.830
I was so nervous I couldn't taste a thing!

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:10.540
What a waste!

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:11.830
Who is this Miki?

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:14.880
The woman in that portrait 
there. She was Johnny's wife.

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.000
"Was?"

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.170
Yes, and she is still always 
with us, here in my heart.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.880
Okay, okay. Enough of that.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:26.790
I think everyone's due for a refill.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.920
Right. Care for another round?

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.460
No, I'm gonna get back in position.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:31.460
Are you, now...

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:35.920
Slapping us on the front page like that
is basically asking for trouble, you see.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.170
I wish we didn't always have to fight.

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:40.790
Don't you fret! I'll keep you safe!

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:42.330
Yeah, you just leave things to us.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:43.880
I feel better already.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:48.530
Still, you wanna change our flight path again
and take the long way around?

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:50.830
Do we really need to go this far?

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.710
We wouldn't be doing it if we didn't have to.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:55.880
Especially not considering 
how much it will cost.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:58.730
What's with all these noises?

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:01.180
Just been having a bit of 
a stomach ache all day.

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:04.500
Why did you take on a job like this, anyway?

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.170
We're transporters.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:09.250
Did you expect me to stand 
in front of the press and say

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.860
"No" after someone asked 
if we can handle this?

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:15.130
Sure, but did you have to turn down
all those escorts, too?

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:17.290
That would just be playing into Isao's hand.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:22.590
If we accepted his help,
they'd take all the credit once we pulled it off.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:23.880
Guess that makes sense.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.000
That grumbling is infuriating.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.000
Feel free to relieve yourself.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:31.130
With pleasure! Can you act as 
first officer while I'm gone?

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.080
Yes, yes.

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:37.790
Multiple bogeys spotted on our eleven.

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:38.880
First Officer!

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:39.880
He's still holed up in the restroom.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:41.670
Are you sure these aren't just aircraft
that are cutting across our path?

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:45.130
They're moving straight at 
us, so that is unlikely.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:46.920
How did they pick up on our trail?

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:50.080
With the First Officer still away,
we await your orders now, Madame.

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:51.790
All pilots prepare for battle!

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:53.460
What?!

00:05:57.170 --> 00:05:58.870
We're up against huge numbers.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:00.540
They sure didn't keep us waiting!

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.880
You're not getting anywhere near our fishy!

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:04.630
Here they come! Look at all of 'em!

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.840
We're looking at what, fifteen or so?

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.630
That's two and a half targets for each of us.

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:10.170
We can handle this!

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.330
Fly high, KOTOBUKI Corps!

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:14.080
Yes ma’am!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:46.670
Oh no, you don't!

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.050
Watch my tail, Emma!

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:49.300
On it already!

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:58.460
Kylie, I'll draw them in.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:06:59.250
You get behind them!

00:06:59.250 --> 00:06:59.830
Roger!

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:06.790
Gah! You're too clever for your own good!

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:12.420
No one likes a man that can't take a hint!

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:19.120
I don't like air pirates that 
can take a hint, either.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:23.380
We have a reading on possible bogeys
pulling in fast from the rear.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.280
Incoming report from the rear watch.

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:27.630
Confirmed sight of enemy craft approaching.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:30.550
It appears they hugged the ground
and flew in under our radar.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:36.770
KOTOBUKI Corps, fall back immediately!

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:38.500
New targets closing in!

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:40.170
Wait, was this just a decoy?!

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:41.080
But there are so many of them!

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:41.880
That's impossible.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:43.710
I've never seen decoys as serious as this!

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:46.130
Usually you'd expect them 
to let up somewhere...

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:46.750
Fall back!

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:47.900
Reona, behind you!

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:50.210
What's with these guys?!

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:52.500
Do they still wanna die even though the
jig is up? How dumb are they?!

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.330
Stay alert! These are no ordinary pirates!

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:57.920
We need to take them out 
before they get us first!

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:21.170
And just who do you think 
is going to fix that?!

00:08:21.170 --> 00:08:22.630
Come on out and fight me!

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:37.750
This is Kylie, Hagoromo, come in!

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:41.450
This is bad, no one's radioing in!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:42.870
Look! The hatch!

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:44.290
Don't tell me...!

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.380
We've been boarded.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:47.630
We took too long dealing with the others.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:51.290
Hagoromo! Cindy! Betti! Addie! Come in!

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:58.960
Oh please, no! I hate guns!

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:03.080
Attention KOTOBUKI Corps.

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:06.580
We have taken control of your airship.

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:09.920
Call off your attack immediately 
and leave this area.

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:12.670
This is corps leader, Reona.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:14.290
What are you after?

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:16.630
What else? The fish.

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:19.790
Your time as a mercenary squad ends today.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:21.080
Now scram.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:24.040
Fall back...

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:24.920
You can't be...!

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:25.750
Reona!

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:26.670
You're just gonna run?!

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:27.960
Do as she says.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:43.970
Now it's your turn.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:45.940
Excuse yourselves from the bridge.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:47.170
Do what he says.

00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:07.620
What a mess!

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:10.360
This is a message to the mayor of Ikesuka.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:13.940
We have taken control of the 
Rahama airship Hagoromo

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:16.400
and are en route to Ikesuka now.

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:21.100
We demand the following from mayor Isao
and the city of Ikesuka.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:24.100
First, that Isao resigns as mayor.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:27.880
Second, that the Brotherhood of Freedom Union
be abolished immediately.

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:29.720
If you refuse to accept 
either of these conditions,

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:32.080
we will crash the Hagoromo into Ikesuka.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:33.420
Setting off a massive explosion.

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:36.790
Here you are.

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:40.290
I don't drink anymore.

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:42.500
"Anymore?" Well why-

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:43.080
Quiet.

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:45.710
Terribly sorry!

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:50.170
Still, you robbers here seem 
almost like military men.

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:52.330
No! I mean that as a compliment!

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:54.420
Who's paying you?

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:57.080
We don't work for anyone!

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:58.750
We're air pirates.

00:10:58.750 --> 00:10:59.750
Fine, then.

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:02.340
I don't care who you are, anyway.

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:06.930
But you will pay for what 
you've done to my crew.

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:11.020
They've really gone and made her mad, now.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:13.040
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:16.120
It seems they haven't changed course.

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:18.000
We should have eyes on them shortly.

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:20.290
There they are.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:27.540
Chika, you're losing altitude.

00:11:28.210 --> 00:11:30.250
Just wanted to see how low I could go!

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:31.630
Must be nice to be so carefree.

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:34.830
Me, I have to deal with 
all this heavy baggage.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.290
That was only in jest.

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:40.220
Just sit tight back there, you two.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:41.880
Oh shut up, Emma.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:44.580
Sorry for roping you into this.

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:46.450
Nah, I volunteered!

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:48.210
You had me surprised, honestly.

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:49.130
Why?

00:11:49.130 --> 00:11:52.790
I didn't figure you had any 
interest in anything but flying.

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:54.330
That's not true! I-

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:54.830
You...?

00:11:58.040 --> 00:12:04.040
Say... Do you do all this for
the kids like Miyuri and all them?

00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:08.580
I need money if I want to keep
that orphanage running, after all.

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:09.970
Yeah...

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:11.540
What's with you all of a sudden, though?

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:13.460
Nothing...

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:17.090
This is the First Officer of the Hagoromo!

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:18.750
First Officer?!

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:21.170
This is the KOTOBUKI Corps!

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:22.550
Is that you, First Officer Saneatsu?

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:24.250
Oh, you're still there! What a relief!

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:26.580
Not really though, we're in a pinch!

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:27.580
They just came outta nowhere-

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:29.040
Right, but what's the situation now?

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:31.250
I can only tell you what I've seen myself.

00:12:31.250 --> 00:12:33.460
But the enemy is fully armed.

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:36.040
And there's gotta be at 
least 12 of them on board.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:37.660
Probably more than that.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:40.380
They've landed three Toryu 
and one Hayate on board.

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:42.570
Wow, I never thought our FO 
would do anything useful!

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:45.040
Every dog has its day!

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:46.880
Target spotted on our five o'clock.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:51.040
Here they come!

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:54.460
We need to make sure we keep 
them good and occupied.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:55.960
It's time for some fancy flying!

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:00.420
I've got eyes.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.170
And we're still in line?

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:02.960
Indeed.

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:06.750
We should be right in
the radar blind spot Addie told me of.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:45.830
I'm off!

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:46.830
Be careful.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:59.660
Hup!

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:01.540
Can you skirt around to the bridge?

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:02.460
I'm on it!

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:06.880
Everything's in place. 
Report to the commander.

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:07.500
Roger!

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:08.960
Are those...?

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:09.960
Explosives.

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:11.630
What are we gonna do? Can you defuse those?

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:12.500
Not a chance.

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:13.830
Let's find Johnny.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:15.500
Why? You need a drink?

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:16.160
No...

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:19.540
There he is.

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:21.670
You stay hidden here.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:22.420
What?

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:32.470
Oh my! I'm so sorry.

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:37.850
Johnny!

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:44.540
Whoa...

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:45.790
Nice one, Ririko.

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:47.210
It was nothing.

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:48.210
You too, Johnny.

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:51.960
With aim like that even rubber bullets
can take 'em down, eh?

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:53.380
I can't believe I shot someone!

00:14:53.380 --> 00:14:56.380
What else do you keep that 
thing back there, for?

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:57.450
It's just a lucky charm!

00:14:57.450 --> 00:15:01.080
With aim like that it's no wonder you used
to be known as the fastest shot around.

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:02.420
Johnny the Uncatchable!

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:04.290
Don't call me that!

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:07.800
I promised Miki I'd never take up arms again!

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:10.580
I'll apologize to Miki for you myself.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:12.080
You can talk to the dead?!

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:12.250
Madame, are you a spirit medium?!

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:13.220
Promise?
Madame, are you a spirit medium?!

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:14.250
I promise.

00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:16.850
So I need you to help us out here.

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:19.920
I do hope you mean it.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:26.880
These are the very same pilots
we were up against in Nanko, aren't they?

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:27.960
Why are they back?

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:28.750
Just by coincidence?

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:30.290
I doubt that.

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:32.360
Either way, just be careful.

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:34.250
One thing we do know is that they're tough.

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:37.130
In a sad turn of events, the 
Hagoromo has been hijacked.

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:39.670
And we can confirm that
they are indeed headed for Ikesuka now.

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:40.830
Are we going to be okay?

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:42.670
Definitely not!

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.230
But turning misfortunes 
like these upside down

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:47.760
is what we of the Brotherhood are here for!

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:50.980
We have been preparing for 
just this sort of event!

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:54.260
To all you reporters who claimed we wasted away
your tax money... Prepare your apologies!

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:58.640
To all my beloved Hagoromo crew.

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:01.290
My apologies for the current situation.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:04.330
But the time to sit patient is now over.

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:06.040
Here it comes, what's the code word?

00:16:06.630 --> 00:16:09.580
The captain takes flight at daybreak.

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:10.540
All right!

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:11.540
Hold it right there!

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:15.830
Spin those inertia handles!

00:16:15.830 --> 00:16:17.080
Roger that!
With pleasure!

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:27.280
Freeze!

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:29.210
Yes! As you wish!

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:02.750
I shot them...

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:14.130
Nice one, Loulou!

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:18.920
Don't you run!

00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:20.600
I'm gonna tear you down and 
beat you back into shape!

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:21.930
Leave them to us!

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:24.960
It's no good! They've cut off 
access to the gas reserves!

00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:27.670
We'll do what we must to fulfill our mission.

00:17:28.130 --> 00:17:29.960
If that means we have to go down too-

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:31.750
It's time you accept defeat.

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:33.420
And it looks like we do!

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:37.460
Get off me!

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:52.000
What kind of brute uses 
real bullets on an airship?

00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:54.300
Is there any way we can land this thing?

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:55.170
None whatsoever.

00:17:55.170 --> 00:17:57.040
The backup system is out, too.

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:59.290
Betti, what's our estimated location?

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:02.460
We are likely 30 kilometers south of Ikesuka.

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:03.880
Johnny, have you dealt with those explosives?

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:06.330
Unfortunately, this isn't looking easy.

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:07.250
My apologies!

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:08.080
How long will it take?

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.380
Roughly...

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:11.630
An hour?

00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:13.630
Can't we turn off the engines manually?

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:14.910
The doors to all the engine rooms

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:17.280
have been destroyed,
and it will take time to get through them!

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:20.000
So we're on a non-stop, out 
of control flight to Ikesuka

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:21.620
with a load of bombs on board?

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:25.420
Kylie!

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:25.950
On it!

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:32.460
Huh?

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:39.080
They're going to run away again?

00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:40.170
How infuriating!

00:18:40.170 --> 00:18:42.460
Yeah, but I'm almost out 
of fuel and ammo too.

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:44.080
I'm just glad we made it through all that!

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:45.170
We may not have.

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:46.790
What the heck is that?

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:48.710
My guess would be the Ikesuka Air Force.

00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:51.330
Or Isao's own air fleet, in other words.

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:52.950
This is the Hagoromo.

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:55.880
Incoming Ikesuka aircraft, do you copy?

00:18:57.710 --> 00:18:59.290
So, why aren't they responding?

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:02.040
My guess is that the moment 
we enter Ikesuka airspace

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:04.540
they are going to shoot us 
down, no questions asked.

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:05.710
You can't be serious...

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:07.880
We're an out of control ship 
stocked with explosives.

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:09.710
That's all the justification they need.

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:11.420
Reona, this is Loulou.

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:12.420
Reona, here.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:13.710
This is an order.

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:15.670
Shoot down the Hagoromo.

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:19.830
Now, I don't want you tearing it apart
and sending it falling.

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:22.160
So what I need you to do is 
make sure we lose just enough

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:23.900
helium to make an emergency landing.

00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:25.130
But that's ridiculous!

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:27.420
Plus, you're packed with explosives, right?

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:28.750
Have you handled those, yet?

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:30.670
No.

00:19:30.670 --> 00:19:31.380
But then...!

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:33.120
I need you to pull this off.

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:34.420
Roger that, Madame!

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:38.740
Get outta here!

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:05.750
All right. Just one more!

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:06.510
Make this one count!

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:07.210
Got it!

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:19.000
We did it!

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:50.460
So Johnny was a real pro mercenary?

00:20:50.460 --> 00:20:52.100
And an excellent one, too.

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:58.960
Then one day he fell in love with a woman named Miki
and decided to leave that life behind.

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:02.210
But Miki's still alive, right?

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:03.960
Why aren't they together?

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:05.130
Well you see...

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:08.130
He put the trade behind him,
but he couldn't get rid of his guns.

00:21:08.130 --> 00:21:13.170
He ended up just expanding his collection instead,
and she ended up growing to resent him.

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.210
What's Ririko's story, then?

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:18.170
Her? She's just your 
ordinary sort of waitress.

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:19.540
You call that ordinary?!

00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:22.880
Please forgive me, Miki. 
I broke my promise...

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:26.210
But I do hope you will still come back to me.

00:21:26.210 --> 00:21:27.680
I'm almost certain she never will.

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:29.390
If you could sign this receipt for me.

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:33.520
For handing over those perps I say thank you,
bless you, and hang me out to dry!

00:21:33.520 --> 00:21:36.880
"Handing them over?"
You basically snatched them away from us.

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:38.880
Oh, but that just sounds awful!

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:41.670
Anywho, excellent work out there!

00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:43.960
We are professionals, you see.

00:21:44.290 --> 00:21:45.000
Let me be clear.

00:21:45.830 --> 00:21:47.960
We will never accept another job from you.

00:21:49.210 --> 00:21:50.920
Do be careful, then.

00:21:51.460 --> 00:21:53.460
Fame isn't always easy, you know.

00:22:04.540 --> 00:22:08.630
Ano sora o jiyuu ni kakenukete mitai to

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:12.460
Hanasaki no kaze ni negai o noseta

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:16.380
Akogare ga keshiki o tsukutteiku

00:22:16.380 --> 00:22:20.790
Ano toki no kaze wa genki kanaa

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:29.130
Nan no tame ni tatakau no kana

00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:33.170
Koko ni iru riyuu wa nan darou?

00:22:33.170 --> 00:22:41.420
Toikaketa sora wa kotaenai kedo

00:22:42.130 --> 00:22:49.080
Bokura wa tsubasa o motteiru

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:53.790
Haruka kanata nageki no shuuchakuten

00:22:53.790 --> 00:22:58.040
Mitsuketa monogataritachi

00:22:58.040 --> 00:23:05.790
Kono sora wa dare ni mo ubaenai

00:23:05.960 --> 00:23:10.500
Boku wa kakeru nanimo kowakunai yo

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:17.670
Shiawase nara koko ni aru yo

00:23:26.080 --> 00:23:27.540
Preview

00:23:33.040 --> 00:23:37.630
Next time on The Magnificent KOTOBUKI,
"The Vagabond Spruce"!

00:23:38.290 --> 00:23:41.040
The Vagabond Spruce
